.com/open5gs/open5gs/discussions/2955\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **worknm** February  6, 2024</sup>\r\nI running open5GS 2.6.6\r\n\r\nSo I the upf.log, as I type this, is looping this warning error:\r\n02/06 17:43:20.381: [upf] WARNING: ogs_tun_read() failed (../src/upf/gtp-path.c:116)\r\n02/06 17:43:20.381: [sock] WARNING: ogs_read() failed (77:File descriptor in bad state) (../lib/tun/tunio.c:39)\r\n\r\nAlso I can't seem to ping through the interface ogstun but I can ping through the ogstun's ip address. Is this how it supposed to be?\r\nWorks - ping google.com -I 10.45.0.1 \r\nDoesn't work - ping google.com -I ogstun\r\n\r\nThe thing is something is strange going on. I could get to the internet yesterday with the UE and GNB but now I can't again. I'm thinking it is with the NAT rules that is in the tutorial because I did a reboot. But I did the below which should have fixed whatever. The only things that seem out of place is the above issues. Any help will be appreciated. Thanks\r\n\r\nsudo ip link delete ogstun\r\nsudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1\r\nsudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_nonlocal_bind=1\r\nsudo ip tuntap add name ogstun mode tun\r\nsudo ip addr add 10.45.0.1/16 dev ogstun\r\nsudo iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 10.45.0.0/16 ! -o ogstun -j MASQUERADE\r\nsudo ip link set ogstun up\r\n\r\n</div>","closed_by":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url"